1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,208
Day five of the
zombie apocalypse.

2
00:00:03,208 --> 00:00:04,937
You've survived
the riots.

3
00:00:04,937 --> 00:00:06,898
You've survived
the infected.

4
00:00:06,898 --> 00:00:08,245
You've even
survived your

5
00:00:08,245 --> 00:00:09,513
neighbor Gary.

6
00:00:09,513 --> 00:00:11,440
Which,
statistically speaking,

7
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:13,450
should've been
impossible.

8
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:15,747
But there's one
tiny problem.

9
00:00:15,747 --> 00:00:17,744
You've been
bitten.

10
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:21,964
Oh, you've gotta
be kidding me.

11
00:00:22,766 --> 00:00:24,984
Hiiii! It's Gary!

12
00:00:24,984 --> 00:00:27,227
And the guy
outside your door?

13
00:00:27,227 --> 00:00:29,677
He got bitten
four days ago.

14
00:00:29,677 --> 00:00:30,652
Yeah.

15
00:00:30,652 --> 00:00:31,813
We should
probably start at

16
00:00:31,813 --> 00:00:33,392
the beginning.

17
00:00:35,342 --> 00:00:36,564
Day one.

18
00:00:36,564 --> 00:00:37,934
The government
tells everyone

19
00:00:37,934 --> 00:00:39,883
to stay indoors.

20
00:00:39,883 --> 00:00:42,263
So naturally,
the entire city

21
00:00:42,263 --> 00:00:44,573
decides to
go shopping.

22
00:00:44,625 --> 00:00:45,923
That doesn't
look good.

23
00:00:45,923 --> 00:00:46,829
Correct.

24
00:00:46,829 --> 00:00:48,675
For once,
your two remaining

25
00:00:48,675 --> 00:00:50,184
brain cells
are working

26
00:00:50,184 --> 00:00:51,635
together.

27
00:00:52,285 --> 00:00:53,852
Unfortunately,
you've got

28
00:00:53,852 --> 00:00:55,095
enough food
to survive

29
00:00:55,095 --> 00:00:57,588
approximately
eleven minutes.

30
00:00:57,588 --> 00:00:59,498
...Great.

31
00:01:00,748 --> 00:01:02,652
Welcome to the
supermarket.

32
00:01:02,652 --> 00:01:04,603
Humanity's final
demonstration

33
00:01:04,603 --> 00:01:06,249
of common sense.

34
00:01:06,249 --> 00:01:09,546
Water. Canned food.
Batteries.

35
00:01:09,546 --> 00:01:10,591
And something
to defend

36
00:01:10,591 --> 00:01:12,129
yourself with.

37
00:01:12,129 --> 00:01:13,023
Good.

38
00:01:13,023 --> 00:01:15,215
You're doing
surprisingly well.

39
00:01:15,215 --> 00:01:16,948
Wait. What's that?

40
00:01:16,948 --> 00:01:18,852
...A rubber duck?

41
00:01:20,010 --> 00:01:22,042
He looked lonely.

42
00:01:22,042 --> 00:01:23,075
Of course.

43
00:01:23,075 --> 00:01:24,782
Emotional
support duck.

44
00:01:24,782 --> 00:01:25,943
Very important
during the

45
00:01:25,943 --> 00:01:28,358
collapse of
civilization.

46
00:01:29,572 --> 00:01:30,728
Gary?

47
00:01:30,728 --> 00:01:32,224
Hiiii!

48
00:01:32,224 --> 00:01:34,498
You seen the
sugar aisle?

49
00:01:35,148 --> 00:01:36,239
You know what?

50
00:01:36,239 --> 00:01:37,981
Shopping's over.

51
00:01:43,531 --> 00:01:46,433
Day two.
The internet is dead.

52
00:01:46,433 --> 00:01:48,163
The streets
are empty.

53
00:01:48,163 --> 00:01:49,278
And somebody's
knocking on

54
00:01:49,278 --> 00:01:50,578
your door at
three in the

55
00:01:50,578 --> 00:01:51,586
morning.

56
00:01:51,586 --> 00:01:52,956
Which is rude.

57
00:01:52,956 --> 00:01:55,530
Even by apocalypse
standards.

58
00:01:55,530 --> 00:01:58,570
Hiii! It's Gary.
From 4B.

59
00:01:58,570 --> 00:02:02,170
Can I borrow
some... sugar?

60
00:02:02,170 --> 00:02:04,332
Gary does not
need sugar.

61
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:06,838
Just a little?

62
00:02:08,108 --> 00:02:09,388
Nope.

63
00:02:09,388 --> 00:02:12,151
A locked door.
A baseball bat.

64
00:02:12,151 --> 00:02:13,440
And a chair.

65
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,077
The three
pillars of modern

66
00:02:15,077 --> 00:02:17,004
home security.

67
00:02:18,226 --> 00:02:20,724
I can hear
you breathing.

68
00:02:20,854 --> 00:02:22,364
...What?

69
00:02:24,762 --> 00:02:26,864
See you tomorrow!

70
00:02:27,905 --> 00:02:28,964
Tomorrow?!

71
00:02:31,714 --> 00:02:33,270
Day three.

72
00:02:33,270 --> 00:02:35,348
You've learned
two things.

73
00:02:35,348 --> 00:02:37,310
Don't trust
your neighbors.

74
00:02:37,310 --> 00:02:38,668
And never trust
anyone who

75
00:02:38,668 --> 00:02:40,700
smiles that much
while asking

76
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:42,006
for sugar.

77
00:02:42,006 --> 00:02:43,887
Unfortunately,
things are

78
00:02:43,887 --> 00:02:45,373
getting worse.

79
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:47,080
Because the
infection isn't

80
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,993
just affecting
people.

81
00:02:48,993 --> 00:02:50,642
Rats. Pigeons.

82
00:02:50,642 --> 00:02:52,847
Even your
adorable little-

83
00:02:53,508 --> 00:02:56,707
Mister Whiskers?

84
00:02:57,037 --> 00:02:59,377
Hey, buddy...

85
00:02:59,377 --> 00:03:00,281
Oh.

86
00:03:00,281 --> 00:03:01,872
Mister Whiskers
has chosen

87
00:03:01,872 --> 00:03:03,346
violence.

88
00:03:05,356 --> 00:03:07,246
AAAAAH!

89
00:03:08,096 --> 00:03:09,768
Wait a minute.

90
00:03:11,418 --> 00:03:12,544
Against all
reasonable

91
00:03:12,544 --> 00:03:13,937
expectations...

92
00:03:13,937 --> 00:03:15,665
the duck
was useful.

93
00:03:15,665 --> 00:03:17,151
Congratulations.

94
00:03:17,151 --> 00:03:18,498
You've lost your
apartment to

95
00:03:18,498 --> 00:03:20,727
a nine-pound cat.

96
00:03:20,745 --> 00:03:21,581
...At least I've
still got the

97
00:03:21,581 --> 00:03:23,687
duck.

98
00:03:28,937 --> 00:03:30,191
Day four.

99
00:03:30,191 --> 00:03:32,617
Your apartment
belongs to the cat.

100
00:03:32,617 --> 00:03:34,045
The streets
belong to the

101
00:03:34,045 --> 00:03:35,125
infected.

102
00:03:35,125 --> 00:03:36,565
And your building
apparently

103
00:03:36,565 --> 00:03:38,223
belongs to Gary.

104
00:03:38,223 --> 00:03:40,073
You've gotta
be kidding me.

105
00:03:40,073 --> 00:03:42,070
You need
somewhere safer.

106
00:03:42,070 --> 00:03:43,544
Fewer entrances.

107
00:03:43,544 --> 00:03:45,762
A clear view of
the surroundings.

108
00:03:45,762 --> 00:03:48,664
And preferably
no cats.

109
00:03:49,914 --> 00:03:51,771
Something's
coming.

110
00:03:53,221 --> 00:03:55,597
Good news.
You can still run.

111
00:03:55,597 --> 00:03:58,290
Bad news.
So can they.

112
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:02,964
For the first time
in four days...

113
00:04:02,964 --> 00:04:04,311
you can actually
see what's

114
00:04:04,311 --> 00:04:05,523
happening.

115
00:04:05,523 --> 00:04:06,405
Okay.

116
00:04:06,405 --> 00:04:07,775
Maybe don't
stand that close

117
00:04:07,775 --> 00:04:08,981
to the edge.

118
00:04:08,981 --> 00:04:10,479
One can of food.

119
00:04:10,479 --> 00:04:12,197
Half a bottle
of water.

120
00:04:12,197 --> 00:04:13,904
And batteries
for a flashlight

121
00:04:13,904 --> 00:04:15,603
you forgot
to bring.

122
00:04:15,603 --> 00:04:16,988
...Seriously?

123
00:04:17,938 --> 00:04:19,993
...survivors...
evacuation...

124
00:04:19,993 --> 00:04:21,131
parking garage...

125
00:04:21,131 --> 00:04:22,557
tomorrow
morning...

126
00:04:22,557 --> 00:04:23,973
An evacuation?

127
00:04:23,973 --> 00:04:26,121
Tomorrow morning?
Well.

128
00:04:26,121 --> 00:04:28,350
That's either
incredibly lucky...

129
00:04:28,350 --> 00:04:30,243
or the worst
idea anyone's had

130
00:04:30,243 --> 00:04:31,541
all week.

131
00:04:31,541 --> 00:04:33,213
...do not
approach anyone

132
00:04:33,213 --> 00:04:35,117
showing signs
of infection...

133
00:04:35,117 --> 00:04:37,950
especially unusual
behavior...

134
00:04:38,033 --> 00:04:39,520
Helloooo?

135
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:41,935
Gary. Of course
it's Gary.

136
00:04:49,285 --> 00:04:52,211
Day five. Your
water is gone.

137
00:04:52,211 --> 00:04:54,614
Your food is
almost gone.

138
00:04:54,614 --> 00:04:55,810
But there's
an evacuation

139
00:04:55,810 --> 00:04:57,898
point a few
blocks away.

140
00:04:57,898 --> 00:04:59,349
All you have
to do...

141
00:04:59,349 --> 00:05:01,613
is get out of
the building.

142
00:05:01,694 --> 00:05:03,903
Mister Whiskers?!

143
00:05:03,903 --> 00:05:06,178
Oh, for crying
out loud.

144
00:05:06,375 --> 00:05:08,348
We can talk
about this.

145
00:05:08,348 --> 00:05:10,113
No, you can't.

146
00:05:12,023 --> 00:05:13,913
AAAAAH!

147
00:05:14,763 --> 00:05:16,603
Oh. That's bad.

148
00:05:16,603 --> 00:05:18,623
Your entire
first aid kit...

149
00:05:18,623 --> 00:05:21,710
is one unicorn
band-aid.

150
00:05:21,710 --> 00:05:23,460
You've gotta
be kidding me.

151
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:25,167
That is
not a cure.

152
00:05:25,167 --> 00:05:26,583
But at least the
unicorn looks

153
00:05:26,583 --> 00:05:28,150
confident.

154
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:32,390
Hello?!
Is anybody up there?!

155
00:05:32,570 --> 00:05:34,420
Please!
I need help!

156
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:36,463
Now you've
got a problem.

157
00:05:36,463 --> 00:05:38,402
Someone needs
your help.

158
00:05:38,402 --> 00:05:39,749
But if that
bite means what

159
00:05:39,749 --> 00:05:41,386
you think
it means...

160
00:05:41,386 --> 00:05:42,350
you might
be the most

161
00:05:42,350 --> 00:05:43,522
dangerous
thing in this

162
00:05:43,522 --> 00:05:44,962
building.

163
00:05:45,088 --> 00:05:47,102
Hey! Up here!

164
00:05:47,952 --> 00:05:49,693
You need a
distraction.

165
00:05:49,693 --> 00:05:50,889
Something loud.

166
00:05:50,889 --> 00:05:53,710
Something completely
ridiculous.

167
00:05:54,073 --> 00:05:56,250
I knew you'd
come in handy.

168
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:59,535
Unbelievable.

169
00:05:59,535 --> 00:06:00,894
The duck has
now saved your

170
00:06:00,894 --> 00:06:02,612
life twice.

171
00:06:05,262 --> 00:06:07,642
Thank you.
Seriously.

172
00:06:07,642 --> 00:06:09,682
You saved my life.

173
00:06:09,682 --> 00:06:10,862
Yeah. No problem.

174
00:06:10,862 --> 00:06:11,294
Wait.

175
00:06:11,294 --> 00:06:13,292
What happened
to your arm?

176
00:06:13,292 --> 00:06:14,061
Nothing.

177
00:06:14,061 --> 00:06:15,262
Is that a bite?

178
00:06:15,262 --> 00:06:16,162
...No?

179
00:06:16,162 --> 00:06:18,844
Excellent.
Very convincing.

180
00:06:18,844 --> 00:06:20,551
You should
consider a career

181
00:06:20,551 --> 00:06:22,201
in politics.

182
00:06:22,201 --> 00:06:23,788
You were bitten?!

183
00:06:23,788 --> 00:06:25,569
It was a cat!

184
00:06:25,569 --> 00:06:27,211
That's worse!

185
00:06:28,413 --> 00:06:30,831
Hiiii! It's Gary!

186
00:06:31,248 --> 00:06:34,611
Oh, not this
guy again.

187
00:06:34,611 --> 00:06:36,041
You know him?

188
00:06:36,041 --> 00:06:37,411
Unfortunately.

189
00:06:37,593 --> 00:06:39,781
Hey! You got
bitten too?

190
00:06:39,781 --> 00:06:40,941
...Too?

191
00:06:40,941 --> 00:06:43,461
Yeah. Day one.

192
00:06:43,461 --> 00:06:44,250
Wait.

193
00:06:44,250 --> 00:06:46,294
Gary got bitten
on day one.

194
00:06:46,294 --> 00:06:48,035
That was four
days ago.

195
00:06:48,035 --> 00:06:50,038
And he's
still talking.

196
00:06:50,038 --> 00:06:52,928
Gary? How are
you still alive?

197
00:06:53,385 --> 00:06:55,658
Funny you
should ask.

198
00:06:55,658 --> 00:06:57,398
You wanna know
something?

199
00:06:57,398 --> 00:06:58,862
I don't think
we're turning

200
00:06:58,862 --> 00:07:00,888
into the
same thing.

201
00:07:03,638 --> 00:07:05,101
Congratulations.

202
00:07:05,101 --> 00:07:07,760
You survived your
first five days.

203
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:09,640
Now you just have
to survive...

204
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:11,422
whatever
comes next.

205
00:07:11,422 --> 00:07:13,837
...evacuation...
noon...

206
00:07:13,837 --> 00:07:16,066
parking garage...
